
Envelope

This is an envelope-based budget.  The idea is that you pre-allocate
funds into the budget, and you should only spend money in a category
if there are available funds to cover it.  All of the balances in
accounts should add up and reconcile to the current balance of the
bank account you're budgeting.

The the current state of this project is very unstable and not all
features have been implemented.

## Running

Tomcat runs in Docker; MariaDB runs natively on the host; the Swing client runs
on the host.  Load sql/bootstrap-mysql.sql into a fresh database first, and apply
anything in sql/migrations to an existing one.

    mvn package                 # builds target/envelope.war and target/envelope-client.jar
    cd docker && docker compose up -d

The server comes up at http://localhost:7041/envelope/ (health check: /envelope/info/ping).
Launch the client with:

    java -jar target/envelope-client.jar

## Default credentials

The bootstrap (sql/bootstrap-mysql.sql) seeds two accounts with these
out-of-the-box passwords — change them after first login:

    admin / envelope
    guest / guest

## Getting the client

The server's front page hands out the client and says how to run it:

    http://<server>:7041/envelope/

It is one runnable jar.  With Java 25 or later installed:

    java -jar envelope-client.jar

## Building an image

    ./build.sh            # builds, tags, and offers to push to registry.lump
    ./build.sh --no-push  # just build

The image builds the war itself, so only docker is needed.  docker/swarm-stack.yml
is the stack definition for the config project; the database is supplied from
outside the stack through the ENVELOPE_* variables it names.
